    {
      "id": "035b78fa-f492-42d6-b4c5-1e2d38b8f3d2",
      "name": "Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -640,
        -736
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 544,
        "height": 976,
        "content": "## ai job application inbox sorter with approval step\n\n### How it works\n1. A Gmail trigger watches a label for incoming applicant mail and normalizes each message into clean fields.\n2. Validation skips notifications and any thread that was already logged, so no candidate gets answered twice.\n3. An AI agent backed by GPT-4o and a structured output parser sorts each email into application, question, or other, and drafts a reply.\n4. Applications stop at a human approval gate: the draft is emailed to the hiring manager with an approval link, never sent automatically.\n5. Questions and general mail get a polite auto-reply, and every processed email is logged to a Google Sheet for audit.\n6. Sentiment checks and an error trigger alert the team on Telegram when a candidate is upset or a node fails.\n\n### Setup\n1. Create a Google Sheet named applicant_log with columns: thread_id, sender, subject, category, sentiment, draft_reply, status, approval_id, received_at.\n2. Add the sheet URL as the RECRUITMENT_LOG_URL env variable in your n8n instance.\n3. Add a Gmail label for incoming applications and paste its ID into the New Candidate Email trigger.\n4. Set MANAGER_EMAIL, COMPANY_EMAIL, APPROVAL_BASE_URL and TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID env variables before activating.\n5. Connect OpenAI and your SMTP credential on the model, approval send, and auto reply nodes.\n6. Approvals are manual on purpose. Only remove the approval gate if you accept the risk of instant AI replies.\n\n### Customization\n- Swap GPT-4o for a cheaper chat model in the GPT-4o Drafting Model node.\n- Change the trigger label or add filters to watch other mailboxes.\n- Add a Slack channel or a second Telegram chat for the urgent alert lane."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "5b70f735-2019-4430-b1ba-57370b5879fe",
      "name": "Triage Section",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
